  "semantics": [
    "Namespace-relative self uses the existing PTRELATIVE-to-PTKNOWN path and selects the exact declaring class before ordinary namespace/import lookup.",
    "Existing nullable recursion and eight ordered two-member class/builtin laws reuse that proof, retaining raw qualification, complete normalized order and source metadata.",
    "Distinct same-class payloads retain their own uninitialized backing slots while existing real reference aliases, ordinary object copies, atomic refused writes, pooled empty-array owners and per-object type-source detachment remain unchanged.",
    "Four original-source agreements cover weak namespace-relative self/int forms and independent strict nullable global-namespace-block and int-first named-namespace forms. All eight builtin alternatives have separate header135 coverage; source4 is not all-eight runtime coverage.",
